        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0042221"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any process that results in a change in state or activity of a cell or an organism (in terms of movement, secretion, enzyme production, gene expression, etc.) as a result of a stimulus by the chemical structure of the anion portion of a dissociated acid (rather than the acid acting as a proton donor). The acid chemical may be in gaseous, liquid or solid form.</obo:IAO_0000115>
