        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process in which a relatively unspecialized cell acquires specialized features of a columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell. A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell is a cell usually found in a two dimensional sheet with a free surface. Columnar/cuboidal epithelial cells take on the shape of a column or cube.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell differentiation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
