        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process in which the structures of a photoreceptor cell are generated and organized. This process occurs while the initially relatively unspecialized cell is acquiring the specialized features of a photoreceptor cell, a sensory cell that reacts to the presence of light. An example of this is found in Drosophila melanogaster.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>photoreceptor development</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>photoreceptor cell morphogenesis</rdfs:label>
