        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any process that modulates the frequency, rate or extent of myotube differentiation. Myotube differentiation is the process in which a relatively unspecialized cell acquires specialized features of a myotube cell. Myotubes are multinucleated cells that are formed when proliferating myoblasts exit the cell cycle, differentiate and fuse.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>regulation of myotube differentiation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
