            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process whose specific outcome is the progression of the primary sexual characteristics over time, from their formation to the mature structures. The primary sexual characteristics are the testes in males and the ovaries in females and they develop in response to sex hormone secretion.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>development of primary sexual characteristics</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
