        <obo:IAO_0000115>The aggregation, arrangement and bonding together of a set of components to form an extracellular vesicular exosome, a membrane-bounded vesicle that is released into the extracellular region by fusion of the limiting endosomal membrane of a multivesicular body with the plasma membrane. Exosomes are defined by their size, which generally ranges from 30 nm to 100 nm.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>extracellular vesicular exosome assembly</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>extracellular exosome assembly</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
