        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The aggregation, arrangement and bonding together of a set of components to form an extracellular vesicular exosome, a membrane-bounded vesicle that is released into the extracellular region by fusion of the limiting endosomal membrane of a multivesicular body with the plasma membrane. Exosomes are defined by their size, which generally ranges from 30 nm to 100 nm.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GOC:mah</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GOC:tfm</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
