            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A bilaterally paired branched artery that originates from the aortic arches and divides into and includes as parts the internal and external carotid arteries[cjm].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>we follow the FMA and treat the artery as a tree-structure - here we include the internal and external as parts. For the part that excludes the branches, see &apos;trunk of common carotid artery&apos;</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>This class represents the adult and developing structures&apos;</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000011>in birds and reptiles, develops from arch III and parts of ventral and dorsal aortae</obo:UBPROP_0000011>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>carotid artery</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_carotid_artery"/>
