        <obo:IAO_0000116>revisit this, see issue #331</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>The muscle cells of the iris are smooth muscle in mammals and amphibians, but are striated muscle in birds and reptiles. Many fish have neither, and, as a result, their irides are unable to dilate and contract, so that the pupil always remains of a fixed size[Romer, via WP]</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>in aves, stromal mesenchymal cells may migrate to the iris and become skeletal</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_muscle"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/280888007"/>
