        <obo:IAO_0000115>The combination of pericardial sac (a double-walled sac containing the heart and the roots of the great vessels) plus fibrous pericardium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Peritoneum that surrounds the heart.[AAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000007>pericardial</obo:UBPROP_0000007>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>In GO the concept of pericardium is developmental implicitly epithelial, but here it represents a multi-tissue structure encompassing the sac (epithelium plus connective) and cavity</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>this class denotes a combination of fibrous PC + PC sac (itself a combination of cavity, epithelium and connective tissue). Many sources use the term &apos;pericardium&apos; to denote either just the serous membrane (ZFA) or the epithelium (GO)</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>we follow FMA in dividing pericardium into pericardial sac and fibrous pericardium</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pericardium"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls/id/C0031050"/>
